From f5cd2ab7237e23aeb70daa3606395d51001bc8a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hecheng Yu <kde-yyds@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 18:54:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] spmi: mtk-pmif: clear observed slave EINT status bits

The chained handler read the SPMI slave interrupt status registers but
never wrote the observed bits back to clear them.  If the PMIC top-level
status read returned 0 (spurious or already-handled interrupt), the
parent SPMI IRQ remained asserted, causing an endless
"top_irq_sts:0x0" loop and a watchdog reboot.

Clear each status register after reading it, before dispatching to the
PMIC IRQ domain.

(cherry picked from commit befbdef3943ec7b1fc4a3d14240aecceaa5c2330)
Link: https://github.com/MT6895-Mainline/linux/commit/befbdef3943ec7b1fc4a3d14240aecceaa5c2330
---
 drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c b/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c
index 1048420b5a..7967eafe2e 100644
--- a/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c
+++ b/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c
@@ -491,6 +491,17 @@ static void mtk_spmi_handle_chained_irq(struct irq_desc *desc)
 	for (i = regidx_min; i <= regidx_max; i++) {
 		u32 val = mtk_spmi_readl(arb, pbus, i);
 
+		if (!val)
+			continue;
+
+		/*
+		 * Clear the observed status bits before handling them.  If a
+		 * spurious/unhandled bit is left set, the parent IRQ stays asserted
+		 * and we get an interrupt storm (seen on MT6895 as endless
+		 * "top_irq_sts:0x0" from the PMIC MFD).
+		 */
+		mtk_spmi_writel(arb, pbus, val, i);
+
 		while (val) {
 			u8 bit = __ffs(val);
 			u8 bank = bit / 7;
-- 
